  "worked_solution": "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{W}^{\u2032}(t)\u2248\\frac{W(t+h)-W(t-h)}{2h},\n$$\n\nat time $t=1.4$ with step size $h=0.2.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{W}^{\u2032}(1.4) & \u2248\\frac{W(1.4+0.2)-W(1.4-0.2)}{2(0.2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{W(1.6)-W(1.2)}{0.4} \\\\  & =\\frac{4.2-5.0}{0.4} \\\\  & =\\frac{-0.8}{0.4} \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the reservoir\u2019s water level at $t=1.4$ is decreasing at approximately $2\\,m$ per hour.",
